            <div xml:id="d855">

                <pb facs="0602" n="530" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg530"/>

                <head>Señor Banuelos to Mr. Perry
                </head>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source">[Translation.]</note>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State, Bureau of Political
                        Affairs</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1865-05-09">May 9, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Most Excellent Sir</hi>: The president of the
                    council of ministers, on the 5th instant, directed this department as
                    follows:</p>
                <p>By her Majesty’s orders, and for the instruction of the department under your
                    charge, I transmit to your excellency copies of the resolutions passed by the
                    Senate and House of Representatives, sympathizing with the United States, and
                    deploring the abominable crime committed upon the person of your worthy
                    President, Mr. Abraham Lincoln. Communicated by royal order, through the
                    minister of state, I transmit them to you, with the said copies, that you may
                    send them to your government.</p>
                <p>God grant you many years.</p>
                <closer>Under Secretary <signed>MIGUEL BANUELOS.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
